            "gxa_01m8f5fms5pk3s5exq"
          ],
          "rationale": "The synthetic APR-18 export gives 75 observed minutes per channel in a 120-minute window. The shared duration is therefore bounded by 30 and 75 minutes. The 9,000 L West total and 8,100 L East total include each channel’s exclusively observed times. The 900 L marginal difference equals the shared difference plus West-only volume minus East-only volume. Either channel can lead on the shared times, and a tie is possible. Defer channel-specific follow-up. The available discharge method can only reproduce the marginal totals, and there is no pending interval record. Reopen if synchronized validity intervals and flow increments or integrable rates become available, or if a verified summary gives the common duration and both volumes over precisely those times. A resolved positive paired difference would support a West follow-up and a negative one an East follow-up. Verified coincidence of all 75 observed minutes would itself establish a 900 L West lead."
        }
      ],
